# apps/web — environment variable reference.
#
# This file documents the runtime env vars that the apps/web Next.js app
# expects. The repo-root `.env.example` carries the canonical reference for
# local dev (Supabase + Auth + Gcal + JARVIS + Voice + App). Copy that one
# to `apps/web/.env.local` for development.
#
# This file adds vars that are specific to deployed surfaces (Vercel cron,
# hosted MCP) which don't have a local-dev equivalent.

# ── MCP / context graph (Phase 999.12) ─────────────────────────────────
# Vercel cron auth (CTX-06 / CTX-07).
# The Vercel scheduler hits /api/cron/snapshot-context with
# `Authorization: Bearer ${CRON_SECRET}` once per day. Generate a long
# random string and set the SAME value in the Vercel project's env vars.
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# Without this set, the cron route returns 500 (fail loud — don't let
# unauthenticated traffic through silently if the secret was forgotten).
CRON_SECRET=

# (No additional MCP env vars are required — bearer tokens for the
# /api/mcp endpoint are minted per-user via /settings/mcp-tokens and live
# in the integration_tokens table, NOT in env.)
